<title>INDIA: India RBI cuts interest on repos to primary dealers.</title>
<headline>India RBI cuts interest on repos to primary dealers.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Thursday it had reduced the interest rate on liquidity support extended by it to primary dealers (PDs).</p>
<p>&quot;Liquidity support against 91-day treasury bills will be provided at 10.5 percent per annum against 11.50 percent,&quot; the RBI said in a statement.</p>
<p>Against government of India dated securities the rate would now be 11.0 percent against 13.0 percent, it added.</p>
<p>The RBI extends support to PDs by way of repos transactions.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
